.TH NCLR-LAB 1 "August 2026" "nclr-lab 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nclr-lab \- research tooling for nclr vendor protocols and profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nclr-lab artifact fetch MANIFEST \-\-store DIR [\-\-accept-source-terms]
.br
.B nclr-lab artifact import MANIFEST SOURCE \-\-store DIR
.br
.B nclr-lab artifact verify MANIFEST (\-\-file FILE|\-\-store DIR)
.br
.B nclr-lab controller [\-\-family NAME]
.br
.B nclr-lab decode CDB [\-\-response HEX]
.br
.B nclr-lab diff TRACE_A TRACE_B [\-\-summary]
.br
.B nclr-lab infer HEX [\-\-command]
.br
.B nclr-lab phison-ps2303 loader-check FILE
.br
.B nclr-lab phison-ps2303 geometry \-\-nand\-id HEX \-\-page\-bytes N \-\-oob\-bytes N \-\-pages\-per\-block N \-\-blocks\-per\-lun N \-\-luns N \-\-column\-address\-cycles N \-\-row\-address\-cycles N \-\-bits\-per\-cell N
.br
.B nclr-lab phison-ps2303 inspect DEVICE \-\-confirm\-research\-device
.br
.B nclr-lab phison-ps2303 enter-bootrom DEVICE \-\-firmware VERSION \-\-confirm\-research\-device
.br
.B nclr-lab phison-ps2303 load DEVICE FILE \-\-firmware VERSION \-\-confirm\-research\-device
.br
.B nclr-lab phison-ps2303 probe-loader DEVICE [\-\-channel N \-\-chip N \-\-read\-onfi] \-\-confirm\-research\-device
.br
.B nclr-lab probe check FILE
.br
.B nclr-lab probe new INFO_JSON \-\-family NAME \-\-controller ID \-\-firmware VERSION \-\-nand\-id HEX [\-o FILE]
.br
.B nclr-lab probe run PROBE DEVICE [\-\-execute \-\-confirm\-research\-device]
.br
.B nclr-lab profile \-\-new [\-\-family NAME] [\-\-controller ID] [\-o FILE]
.br
.B nclr-lab profile \-\-check [\-\-pre\-hil \-\-artifact\-dir DIR ...] FILE
.br
.B nclr-lab recipe \-\-profile PROFILE \-\-file RECIPE
.br
.B nclr-lab replay TRACE [\-\-execute] [\-\-confirm-sacrificial]
.br
.B nclr-lab tool PATH [\-\-family NAME] [\-\-include\-unmatched]
.br
.B nclr-lab cap \-\-bus N [\-o FILE]
.br
.B nclr-lab trace CAPTURE.pcapng [\-o TRACE.ndjson]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nclr-lab
is a separate research tool package. Protocol inference and replay do not
share destructive handlers with
.BR nclr run .
The size, SHA-256 and format verifier is intentionally shared so both tools
authenticate identical artifact bytes. Unknown write commands are never
brute-forced; replay defaults to a dry run and requires an explicit
sacrificial-device confirmation to send read-only commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B artifact fetch|import|verify
Acquire or import exact vendor bytes without redistributing them. The
manifest pins controller, firmware, NAND id, size, SHA-256, format, HTTPS
source and terms. Non-redistributable downloads require
\-\-accept-source-terms. Objects are stored as DIR/id/sha256 and are never
executed by this command.
.TP
.B controller [\-\-family NAME]
Show all registered controller families, fixed read-only probe coverage,
recipe-engine coverage and whether a production tuple is bundled. Catalog
coverage is not a C3/C4 capability claim.
.TP
.B decode [\-\-lenient] CDB [RESPONSE_HEX]
Decode a hex SCSI CDB (e.g. "48 03 00 00 00 02") into a structured
description; optionally attach a hex response. \-\-lenient tolerates
unknown opcodes and short payloads.
.TP
.B diff TRACE_A TRACE_B
Compare two NDJSON traces (opcode/status/response differences).
.TP
.B infer HEX
Heuristics over a byte sequence: role, length, endianness candidates,
checksum candidates (sum/xor/crc16), tail sequence.
.TP
.B phison-ps2303 loader-check FILE
Authenticate the exact locally reproduced PS2303 volatile loader by reviewed
size, SHA-256 and strict BtPramCd structure. No hardware command is sent.
.TP
.B phison-ps2303 geometry [OPTIONS]
Encode and validate a 40-byte non-ONFI geometry payload. The geometry is bound
to an exact six-byte NAND id, includes an ONFI-polynomial CRC, and is rejected
when its raw page or address space exceeds the reviewed loader bounds. The
command prints the exact CDB and payload without accessing hardware.
.TP
.B phison-ps2303 inspect DEVICE \-\-confirm\-research\-device
On macOS, obtain exclusive SCSITask access and read the signed PS2251 version
page. Only the reviewed PS2303 controller id is accepted. The target must be
an unmounted, removable, non-system USB whole disk.
.TP
.B phison-ps2303 enter-bootrom DEVICE [OPTIONS]
After exact PS2303 controller and firmware validation, send the reviewed
volatile BootROM transition command. Re-enumeration is expected. This changes
controller state but does not write NAND or authorize purge.
.TP
.B phison-ps2303 load DEVICE FILE [OPTIONS]
In exact PS2303 BootROM mode, transfer and run only the loader accepted by
.BR "phison-ps2303 loader-check" .
The live controller id and exact firmware must match before transfer. The
loader is volatile, re-enumeration is expected, and no NAND erase/program
command is exposed by this research command.
.TP
.B phison-ps2303 probe-loader DEVICE [OPTIONS]
Authenticate the running loader signature/schema, verify its operation
sequence, read the selected channel/chip six-byte NAND id and, when
.B \-\-read\-onfi
is supplied, require a CRC-valid ONFI parameter copy. Raw reads from this
loader deliberately have no trusted ECC verdict, so this command cannot
qualify C4 or authorize purge.
.TP
.B probe check FILE
Validate one exact read-only probe profile. It must bind a complete USB
descriptor plus SCSI INQUIRY tuple to exactly two fixed device-to-host
commands, signed response envelopes, exact controller identity and exact
NAND identity. It has no trust or destructive capability.
.TP
.B probe new INFO_JSON [OPTIONS]
Generate an incomplete probe profile from the exact bootstrap collected by
.BR "nclr info -j" .
The command, response, trace digest and source placeholders must be replaced
from a captured vendor-tool read before
.B probe check
will accept it.
.TP
.B probe run FILE DEVICE [\-\-execute \-\-confirm\-research\-device]
Match the profile against the currently attached whole disk and print the
two exact reads without sending them. On macOS, explicit execution requires
both flags, a removable non-system target with no holders, an unmounted
complete disk and exclusive SCSITask access. Only 6, 10, 12 and 16-byte CDBs
are supported by Apple's interface. Both full responses and identity payloads
must match; the command never enables purge.
.TP
.B profile \-\-new
Generate a controller profile template (research trust by default).
.TP
.B profile \-\-check [\-\-pre\-hil \-\-artifact\-dir DIR ...] FILE
Validate a profile against the schema. With
.B \-\-pre\-hil
the profile must satisfy every production requirement except independent HIL
qualification. Every non-qualification artifact is then opened from the
content-addressed stores, checked by size/SHA-256/format, and the exact runtime
recipe is parsed and semantically validated. Passing this check does not
change profile trust or authorize execution.
.TP
.B recipe \-\-profile PROFILE \-\-file RECIPE
Authenticate the recipe using the profile-pinned size, SHA-256 and format,
then validate its exact controller/firmware/NAND binding, bounded CDB and
response fields, NAND geometry, BBT/FTL/capacity layouts, qualification and
USB re-enumeration policy. This does not execute a command.
.TP
.B replay [\-\-device\-fd N] [\-\-execute] TRACE
Replay read-only commands from a trace. Dry-run by default; write commands
are always skipped; execution requires \-\-execute and
\-\-confirm-sacrificial (Linux SG_IO). \-\-device\-fd N sends the trace
commands to an open device fd instead of opening one itself.
.TP
.B cap \-\-bus N
Capture USB traffic from Linux usbmon (root required; not available on
macOS).
.TP
.B trace CAPTURE.pcapng
Use TShark to decode raw bulk endpoint payloads and validate USB Mass Storage
Bulk-Only Transport CBW/data/CSW sequences. Output is normalized NDJSON.
Payload bytes are represented by SHA-256 only unless both
\-\-include-payload and \-\-confirm-sensitive-payload are supplied. The
offline conversion is supported on macOS.
.TP
.B tool PATH [\-\-family NAME] [\-\-include\-unmatched]
Recursively hash and statically inspect a downloaded vendor executable,
extracted archive tree, loader or source file without executing it. Public
protocol constants, dynamic SanDisk U3 x86 constructor patterns, family
inventory strings and cross-family NAND/BBT/ECC/loader research markers are
reported with offsets and provenance. Schema 2 also parses active SMI FFW
assignments into exact controller/six-byte-NAND bindings, resolves referenced
artifacts by hash without choosing ambiguous duplicates, distinguishes
duplicate paths with byte-identical content, extracts Alcor
six-byte FIDs, and preserves CTL-generation module parameters without
inventing their semantics. Conflicting SMI keys and missing or ambiguous
artifacts remain explicit. Every result is a candidate only and is never
production-eligible.
.SH SAFETY
Write-command brute forcing is prohibited. Read-only and state-changing
commands are classified separately in the output. Research profiles are
never usable by the core's destructive run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 64 usage; 69 unsupported platform/feature; 74 I/O; 77 safety
interlock.
